{
  "slug": "real-estate-framework",
  "name": "Real Estate Framework",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Korean real estate decision meta-router — 9 frameworks (Hedonic Pricing, DiPasquale-Wheaton 4-Quadrant, Alonso-Muth-Mills, Cap Rate/DCF, Harrison 18.6-Year Cycle, Highest & Best Use, Redevelopment Feasibility, Korean Subscription Points, Gap Investment). Built on Korean real estate regime including jeonse (rental deposit system), HUG insurance rules, and redevelopment procedures. NOT real estate advice. Invoke /realty.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **10 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (10): `realty` (Korean real estate meta-router — classifies the situation and auto-selects one or more of 9 frameworks (academic theory,…), `alonso-muth-mills` (Alonso-Muth-Mills location theory — models the trade-off between downtown accessibility and housing cost via the bid-rent curve), `cap-rate-dcf` (Cap Rate / DCF — Valuation of income-producing real estate (retail, office, studio apartments, small buildings) using NOI…), `dipasquale-wheaton` (DiPasquale-Wheaton 4-Quadrant Model — visualizes how the rental market, asset market, construction market, and stock market interlock to…), `gap-investment` (Gap Investment Structure — a housing investment model using jeonse (전세) leverage), `harrison-cycle` (Harrison 18.6-Year Property Cycle — the hypothesis that land prices drive the economic cycle), `hedonic-pricing` (Hedonic Pricing Model — decompose real estate prices into implicit prices by attribute (school district / proximity to…), `highest-best-use` (Highest & Best Use (최유효이용) — determine the optimal use of land and buildings using four criteria: legal…), and 2 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install real-estate-framework@claude-community` from `ironyjk/real-estate-framework`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "skill",
